+### Rotating the password
+
+To change the `password` without signing everyone out, pass a list of passwords. The first one seals sessions, and every password in the list can open them, tried in order.
+
+```js
+const session = await useSession(event, {
+  password: [process.env.SESSION_PASSWORD_NEW, process.env.SESSION_PASSWORD_OLD],
+});
+```
+
+Sessions sealed with the old password keep working, and they are sealed with the new one the next time they are written. Each password must be at least 32 characters and the list cannot be empty.
+
+> [!WARNING]
+> Keep the list short, since a cookie that no password opens costs one key derivation per password. An old password stays valid while it is listed, so remove it once the sessions sealed with it have expired.
+
 ## Get Data from a Session
 
 To get data from a session, we will still use `useSession`. Under the hood, it will use `getSession` to get the session.
